m","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"executionCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of batch executions that have been started"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"failedItems"},{"type":"text","value":": Array of items that failed during batch processing"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isEmpty"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the batcher has no items to process (items array is empty)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isExecuting"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether a batch is currently being processed asynchronously"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPending"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the batcher is waiting for the timeout to trigger batch processing"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"items"},{"type":"text","value":": Array of items currently queued for batch processing"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastResult"},{"type":"text","value":": The result from the most recent batch execution"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"settleCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of batch executions that have completed (either successfully or with errors)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of items currently in the batch queue"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":": Current processing status - 'idle' when not processing, 'pending' when waiting for timeout, 'executing' when processing, 'populated' when items are present, but no wait is configured"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"successCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of batch executions that have completed successfully"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"totalItemsFailed"},{"type":"text","value":": Total number of items that have failed processing across all batches"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"totalItemsProcessed"},{"type":"text","value":": Total number of items that have been processed across all batches"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options-and-ownership","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options and ownership"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass an options object with property getters or a factory. Top-level properties are read\nreactively; function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider\ndefaults. Updates retain the utility, its store, counters, and pending work.\nDestroying the component calls cancel() and abort().\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the same adapter instance. A custom callback\nmust perform all required cleanup. Use flush() where supported to finish pending work."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"items"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function executed by the utility."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/SveltePacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SveltePacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/SvelteAsyncBatcherOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SvelteAsyncBatcherOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">> = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core options or a reactive factory, plus an optional onUnmount callback."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Selects state that updates the owner. Omit to leave selected state empty."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/SvelteAsyncBatcher.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SvelteAsyncBatcher"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The retained utility instance with selected state and child subscriptions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createAsyncBatcher } from '@tanstack/svelte-pacer'\n\nconst utility = createAsyncBatcher(\n  async (items: Array<string>) => { console.log(items) },\n  { maxSize: 5, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ size: state.size }),\n)\nutility.addItem('item')\n// Selected state: utility.state.size","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"state-and-subscriptions","text":"State and subscriptions","level":2},{"id":"options-and-ownership","text":"Options and ownership","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createAsyncBatcher<TValue, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options?,\nselector?): SvelteAsyncBatcher<TValue, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/svelte-pacer/src/async-batcher/createAsyncBatcher.ts:95](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/svelte-pacer/src/async-batcher/createAsyncBatcher.ts#L95)\n\nCreates and retains the AsyncBatcher for its Svelte owner.\n\nCollects items and processes them together when maxSize, wait, or getShouldExecute triggers a batch. Use addItem to accumulate work and flush to process a partial batch.\n\nThe callback may return a Promise. Core result, error, retry, and abort behavior is preserved.\nUse onSuccess, onError, and onSettled for execution outcomes.\n\n## State and subscriptions\n\nPass a selector to track only the state consumed by the owner. The default selection is {},\nso utility state changes do not update the owner unless it opts in. Selection uses shallow\ncomparison. The raw store remains available for additional subscriptions.\nRead selected state through utility.state. Use utility.Subscribe with a children snippet\nto select state in a child without updating the owner.\n\nAvailable state fields:\n\n- `errorCount`: Number of batch executions that have resulted in errors\n- `executionCount`: Number of batch executions that have been started\n- `failedItems`: Array of items that failed during batch processing\n- `isEmpty`: Whether the batcher has no items to process (items array is empty)\n- `isExecuting`: Whether a batch is currently being processed asynchronously\n- `isPending`: Whether the batcher is waiting for the timeout to trigger batch processing\n- `items`: Array of items currently queued for batch processing\n- `lastResult`: The result from the most recent batch execution\n- `settleCount`: Number of batch executions that have completed (either successfully or with errors)\n- `size`: Number of items currently in the batch queue\n- `status`: Current processing status - 'idle' when not processing, 'pending' when waiting for timeout, 'executing' when processing, 'populated' when items are present, but no wait is configured\n- `successCount`: Number of batch executions that have completed successfully\n- `totalItemsFailed`: Total number of items that have failed processing across all batches\n- `totalItemsProcessed`: Total number of items that have been processed across all batches\n\n## Options and ownership\n\nPass an options object with property getters or a factory. Top-level properties are read\nreactively; function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider\ndefaults. Updates retain the utility, its store, counters, and pending work.\nDestroying the component calls cancel() and abort().\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the same adapter instance. A custom callback\nmust perform all required cleanup. Use flush() where supported to finish pending work.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`items`) => `Promise`\\<`any`\\>\n\nFunction executed by the utility.\n\n### options?\n\n[`SveltePacerOptions`](../type-aliases/SveltePacerOptions.md)\\<[`SvelteAsyncBatcherOptions`](../interfaces/SvelteAsyncBatcherOptions.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\\> = `{}`\n\nCore options or a reactive factory, plus an optional onUnmount callback.\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\nSelects state that updates the owner. Omit to leave selected state empty.\n\n## Returns\n\n[`SvelteAsyncBatcher`](../interfaces/SvelteAsyncBatcher.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\n\nThe retained utility instance with selected state and child subscriptions.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { createAsyncBatcher } from '@tanstack/svelte-pacer'\n\nconst utility = createAsyncBatcher(\n  async (items: Array<string>) => { console.log(items) },\n  { maxSize: 5, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ size: state.size }),\n)\nutility.addItem('item')\n// Selected state: utility.state.size\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createAsyncBatcher\ntitle: createAsyncBatcher\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createAsyncBatcher<TValue, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options?,\nselector?): SvelteAsyncBatcher<TValue, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/svelte-pacer/src/async-batcher/createAsyncBatcher.ts:95](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/svelte-pacer/src/async-batcher/createAsyncBatcher.ts#L95)\n\nCreates and retains the AsyncBatcher for its Svelte owner.\n\nCollects items and processes them together when maxSize, wait, or getShouldExecute triggers a batch. Use addItem to accumulate work and flush to process a partial batch.\n\nThe callback may return a Promise. Core result, error, retry, and abort behavior is preserved.\nUse onSuccess, onError, and onSettled for execution outcomes.\n\n## State and subscriptions\n\nPass a selector to track only the state consumed by the owner. The default selection is {},\nso utility state changes do not update the owner unless it opts in. Selection uses shallow\ncomparison. The raw store remains available for additional subscriptions.\nRead selected state through utility.state. Use utility.Subscribe with a children snippet\nto select state in a child without updating the owner.\n\nAvailable state fields:\n\n- `errorCount`: Number of batch executions that have resulted in errors\n- `executionCount`: Number of batch executions that have been started\n- `failedItems`: Array of items that failed during batch processing\n- `isEmpty`: Whether the batcher has no items to process (items array is empty)\n- `isExecuting`: Whether a batch is currently being processed asynchronously\n- `isPending`: Whether the batcher is waiting for the timeout to trigger batch processing\n- `items`: Array of items currently queued for batch processing\n- `lastResult`: The result from the most recent batch execution\n- `settleCount`: Number of batch executions that have completed (either successfully or with errors)\n- `size`: Number of items currently in the batch queue\n- `status`: Current processing status - 'idle' when not processing, 'pending' when waiting for timeout, 'executing' when processing, 'populated' when items are present, but no wait is configured\n- `successCount`: Number of batch executions that have completed successfully\n- `totalItemsFailed`: Total number of items that have failed processing across all batches\n- `totalItemsProcessed`: Total number of items that have been processed across all batches\n\n## Options and ownership\n\nPass an options object with property getters or a factory. Top-level properties are read\nreactively; function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider\ndefaults. Updates retain the utility, its store, counters, and pending work.\nDestroying the component calls cancel() and abort().\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the same adapter instance. A custom callback\nmust perform all required cleanup. Use flush() where supported to finish pending work.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`items`) => `Promise`\\<`any`\\>\n\nFunction executed by the utility.\n\n### options?\n\n[`SveltePacerOptions`](../type-aliases/SveltePacerOptions.md)\\<[`SvelteAsyncBatcherOptions`](../interfaces/SvelteAsyncBatcherOptions.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\\> = `{}`\n\nCore options or a reactive factory, plus an optional onUnmount callback.\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\nSelects state that updates the owner. Omit to leave selected state empty.\n\n## Returns\n\n[`SvelteAsyncBatcher`](../interfaces/SvelteAsyncBatcher.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\n\nThe retained utility instance with selected state and child subscriptions.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { createAsyncBatcher } from '@tanstack/svelte-pacer'\n\nconst utility = createAsyncBatcher(\n  async (items: Array<string>) => { console.log(items) },\n  { maxSize: 5, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ size: state.size }),\n)\nutility.addItem('item')\n// Selected state: utility.state.size\n```\n"}
